1
00:00:02,910 --> 00:00:03,600
Hey!

2
00:00:03,970 --> 00:00:05,920
You were right to come to
my mother for advice.

3
00:00:05,940 --> 00:00:08,240
With ten years of experience being nosy,

4
00:00:09,010 --> 00:00:10,010
my mom

5
00:00:10,040 --> 00:00:12,220
is practically an all-knowing deity.

6
00:00:12,990 --> 00:00:15,410
Even an all-knowing deity
can't compare to "All-Knowing Duang."

7
00:00:16,270 --> 00:00:17,000
All-knowing Duang.

8
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:17,720
- Yes?
- Oh?

9
00:00:17,850 --> 00:00:19,010
You know everything?

10
00:00:19,040 --> 00:00:19,690
Everything.

11
00:00:20,430 --> 00:00:21,700
- You know about women?
- Of course.

12
00:00:21,850 --> 00:00:23,060
- You know about men?
- Of course.

13
00:00:23,220 --> 00:00:25,040
Then do you know
where your husband is?

14
00:00:25,090 --> 00:00:26,370
Go ask your father.

15
00:00:26,510 --> 00:00:27,410
- Whoa...
- Hey.

16
00:00:27,430 --> 00:00:29,050
All-knowing Dolly was just kidding.

17
00:00:29,070 --> 00:00:31,010
Don't crash out yet.

18
00:00:31,030 --> 00:00:32,570
Let's not joke around.

19
00:00:32,619 --> 00:00:33,630
Please help us out first.

20
00:00:33,820 --> 00:00:36,140
We've stared at this footage
until our eyes hurt,

21
00:00:36,250 --> 00:00:39,330
but we still can't tell who the person is.

22
00:00:39,350 --> 00:00:40,480
Leave it to me.

23
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:41,050
Alright.

24
00:00:41,280 --> 00:00:42,560
If they live in this dorm,

25
00:00:42,580 --> 00:00:45,300
I can identify them
and their room by their leg hair.

26
00:00:45,550 --> 00:00:46,930
Whoa...

27
00:00:46,960 --> 00:00:48,560
- We're on the right track.
- Ooh, there's hope.

28
00:00:49,030 --> 00:00:49,670
Alright, alright.

29
00:00:49,710 --> 00:00:50,230
Let's see.

30
00:01:08,830 --> 00:01:10,480
Oh, she's good at this.

31
00:01:11,590 --> 00:01:12,380
You know who they are, right?

32
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:13,039
Not at all.

33
00:01:13,060 --> 00:01:14,060
- Huh?
- What?

34
00:01:14,350 --> 00:01:16,300
They covered themselves completely.

35
00:01:16,470 --> 00:01:19,450
I can't even spot a single leg hair,
so how would I know who they are?

36
00:01:19,630 --> 00:01:20,480
Mm...

37
00:01:20,880 --> 00:01:22,420
Aren't there any other camera angles?

38
00:01:22,590 --> 00:01:24,250
The hard drive was damaged.

39
00:01:24,510 --> 00:01:26,990
The handyman said we're lucky
to have recovered this footage at all.

40
00:01:27,010 --> 00:01:27,850
Oh...

41
00:01:28,039 --> 00:01:29,320
They look familiar, though.

42
00:01:29,440 --> 00:01:30,230
- Hm?
- Yeah?

43
00:01:30,250 --> 00:01:31,700
I think I saw

44
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:35,050
someone dressed like this
when Dollar forced me to work out.

45
00:01:35,560 --> 00:01:36,250
Oh?

46
00:01:40,289 --> 00:01:41,220
Oh!

47
00:01:41,240 --> 00:01:42,060
I remember now.

48
00:01:44,900 --> 00:01:46,380
He lives in Room 407.

49
00:01:46,620 --> 00:01:47,750
- What?!
- Huh?!

50
00:01:48,020 --> 00:01:48,900
Are you sure?

51
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:49,640
I am.

52
00:01:49,800 --> 00:01:51,830
I still vividly remember

53
00:01:51,850 --> 00:01:53,240
seeing that thing dangling

54
00:01:53,380 --> 00:01:55,320
as I ran past him.

55
00:01:55,450 --> 00:01:56,490
- What?!
- Huh?!

56
00:01:56,509 --> 00:01:57,320
What was dangling?

57
00:01:57,340 --> 00:01:59,420
A keychain with a room number tag.

58
00:01:59,440 --> 00:02:00,640
- Oh...
- Oh...

59
00:02:00,660 --> 00:02:01,370
A room number tag.

60
00:02:01,390 --> 00:02:02,880
You said something was dangling,
so I thought you meant eggs.

61
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:03,930
- What?!
- Huh?!

62
00:02:03,990 --> 00:02:04,780
What eggs?

63
00:02:04,800 --> 00:02:05,690
Boiled eggs.

64
00:02:05,710 --> 00:02:07,240
Runners tend to
bring them along when they run.

65
00:02:07,260 --> 00:02:08,050
- Oh...
- Oh...

66
00:02:08,070 --> 00:02:09,449
- Eating it as they run?
- Eating it as they run.

67
00:02:09,470 --> 00:02:10,090
Probably two eggs.

68
00:02:10,110 --> 00:02:12,490
Dobby, you do not need
to ask them anything else.

69
00:02:12,750 --> 00:02:14,650
Knowing the room number is enough.

70
00:02:16,210 --> 00:02:17,030
Ms. Danis,

71
00:02:17,050 --> 00:02:19,000
do you know the tenant in Room 407?

72
00:02:20,350 --> 00:02:21,700
I've heard of him, though.

73
00:02:21,950 --> 00:02:23,640
He's a loner.

74
00:02:23,660 --> 00:02:25,450
And whenever he goes anywhere,

75
00:02:25,930 --> 00:02:27,190
he drags a suitcase along.

76
00:02:27,430 --> 00:02:29,390
- A huge one, too.
- Mm.

77
00:02:29,410 --> 00:02:30,600
I don't know where he's going.

78
00:02:30,930 --> 00:02:31,940
Sadhu!

79
00:02:32,160 --> 00:02:36,250
I hope we finally find Grandma Gaysorn.

80
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:37,510
If we do meet her,

81
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:41,410
I'll have my mom
do a pole dance for Gramps.

82
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:42,780
What do you mean, pole dance?

83
00:02:42,910 --> 00:02:43,960
I'm your mother,

84
00:02:43,980 --> 00:02:45,320
not a suckling pig
from Uncle Rong's Kitchen.

85
00:02:45,710 --> 00:02:46,770
Are you crazy?

86
00:02:46,790 --> 00:02:47,250
Let's go.

87
00:02:47,270 --> 00:02:48,230
Let's go to Room 407.

88
00:02:48,250 --> 00:02:49,300
- Let's go to Ratchaburi.
- What?

89
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:50,300
To the pig at Uncle Rong's Kitchen.

90
00:02:50,480 --> 00:02:51,200
Why are we going there?

91
00:02:51,310 --> 00:02:51,829
Why not?

92
00:02:51,850 --> 00:02:53,430
Well, everyone who ate there got diarrhea.

93
00:02:53,710 --> 00:02:54,930
- What?
- What?

94
00:02:54,950 --> 00:02:56,520
Uh, but they've fixed the recipe.

95
00:02:56,540 --> 00:02:58,190
Not as many people get diarrhea now.

96
00:03:02,650 --> 00:03:06,180
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

97
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:10,460
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

98
00:03:12,480 --> 00:03:18,750
♫Every step we take has a meaning♫

99
00:03:19,620 --> 00:03:24,790
♫No path is ever meaningless♫

100
00:03:26,810 --> 00:03:33,130
♫As long as our hearts keep searching♫

101
00:03:33,900 --> 00:03:38,380
♫One day, we'll find
what we're yearning for♫

102
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:42,030
♫Walking alone is fine,
but it's better when you're by my side♫

103
00:03:42,050 --> 00:03:45,620
♫It won't be lonely
when you're here to walk beside♫

104
00:03:45,640 --> 00:03:48,380
♫Like a love that waits, waits at the D Dorm♫

105
00:03:49,210 --> 00:03:51,300
♫Like a love that remains,
remains at the dorm♫

106
00:03:51,320 --> 00:03:58,570
♫Meaningful love and good things
await on every path♫

107
00:03:58,590 --> 00:04:05,770
♫It might not be a coincidence
that we get to meet♫

108
00:04:05,790 --> 00:04:12,970
♫There might be hidden meanings
on the path beneath our feet♫

109
00:04:12,990 --> 00:04:20,190
♫Perhaps the D Dorm
is what led me to meet you♫

110
00:04:20,220 --> 00:04:23,880
[The D Dorm]

111
00:04:32,650 --> 00:04:33,850
Maybe no one's home.

112
00:04:34,260 --> 00:04:35,050
Should we...

113
00:04:35,340 --> 00:04:36,460
leave him a note?

114
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:37,450
That way, he can get back to us.

115
00:04:37,700 --> 00:04:38,960
Didn't Ms. Danis say

116
00:04:39,150 --> 00:04:42,250
the tenant in this room
carries a huge suitcase everywhere?

117
00:04:42,540 --> 00:04:43,430
What if he's gone for a month?

118
00:04:43,450 --> 00:04:44,280
Oh, right...

119
00:04:44,520 --> 00:04:45,500
Don't worry.

120
00:04:46,390 --> 00:04:47,220
Here.

121
00:04:49,100 --> 00:04:50,170
I have the spare keys.

122
00:04:50,190 --> 00:04:51,420
- Let's just unlock it, then.
- Yeah.

123
00:04:55,620 --> 00:04:56,650
Yes, Director?

124
00:04:57,040 --> 00:04:58,150
There's a retake today?

125
00:04:59,320 --> 00:05:00,480
I won't be able to make it.

126
00:05:01,300 --> 00:05:03,250
I have something important
to help my best friend with.

127
00:05:03,270 --> 00:05:04,480
Mm, well said.

128
00:05:05,050 --> 00:05:05,980
Thanks, my dude.

129
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:07,270
You're paying me 3,000?!

130
00:05:07,450 --> 00:05:09,160
Oh... He isn't my best friend.

131
00:05:09,250 --> 00:05:10,220
We're not that close.

132
00:05:12,820 --> 00:05:13,640
Dobby, I have to go.

133
00:05:14,020 --> 00:05:15,160
What? Dax?!

134
00:05:15,470 --> 00:05:16,300
Dax!

135
00:05:16,320 --> 00:05:18,850
Some friend you have, huh?

136
00:05:18,870 --> 00:05:20,460
Money really talks, doesn't it?

137
00:05:21,680 --> 00:05:22,500
How about this?

138
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:26,160
I will check inside the room first.

139
00:05:26,180 --> 00:05:27,110
Go on, Grandpa.

140
00:05:30,250 --> 00:05:31,790
Why is this room so empty?

141
00:05:32,220 --> 00:05:35,240
There's barely anything here.
Does anyone even live here?

142
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:37,200
There is not even a single photo.

143
00:05:38,360 --> 00:05:42,040
How would I know
if he is related to Gaysorn?

144
00:05:43,150 --> 00:05:45,110
Why is this so stiff?

145
00:05:56,880 --> 00:05:58,760
A killer...

146
00:06:00,170 --> 00:06:01,670
Got it open.

147
00:06:02,210 --> 00:06:04,750
We are screwed!

148
00:06:08,570 --> 00:06:09,710
Dobby, run!

149
00:06:09,750 --> 00:06:10,410
Run!

150
00:06:10,430 --> 00:06:11,140
Run from what, Grandpa?

151
00:06:11,160 --> 00:06:12,830
There is a killer in there.

152
00:06:13,620 --> 00:06:14,550
Run!

153
00:06:14,570 --> 00:06:15,970
- A killer?
- A killer!

154
00:06:15,990 --> 00:06:16,460
Run!

155
00:06:16,480 --> 00:06:16,990
Whoa.

156
00:06:17,440 --> 00:06:19,150
Come on, Grandpa!

157
00:06:28,740 --> 00:06:29,750
- Grandpa.
- Mm.

158
00:06:30,040 --> 00:06:31,760
Someone was standing
in the bathroom with a knife?

159
00:06:31,780 --> 00:06:32,550
Mm.

160
00:06:32,760 --> 00:06:33,900
Are you sure you weren't seeing things?

161
00:06:33,920 --> 00:06:35,120
I am sure of it.

162
00:06:35,140 --> 00:06:36,830
I saw him with my own eyes.

163
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:38,710
He was hiding in the bathroom.

164
00:06:38,750 --> 00:06:41,070
When you tried to open the door,

165
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:42,760
he grabbed the knife...

166
00:06:42,780 --> 00:06:44,470
and got ready to stab you.

167
00:06:44,820 --> 00:06:45,590
Why...

168
00:06:45,770 --> 00:06:47,110
did he want to stab me, though?

169
00:06:47,159 --> 00:06:48,310
How would I know?!

170
00:06:49,310 --> 00:06:51,200
He might've gotten annoyed

171
00:06:51,220 --> 00:06:53,220
because you kept knocking

172
00:06:53,240 --> 00:06:54,310
on his door.

173
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:56,760
You had better stay away from that room.

174
00:06:56,780 --> 00:06:59,510
Then how are we supposed to
find out about Grandma Gaysorn?

175
00:06:59,810 --> 00:07:00,910
Because he...

176
00:07:01,110 --> 00:07:03,430
was the one who dropped her photo.

177
00:07:04,830 --> 00:07:06,160
I think the tenant in that room

178
00:07:06,880 --> 00:07:08,420
is dangerous.

179
00:07:10,830 --> 00:07:12,510
I do not want you to risk it.

180
00:07:19,600 --> 00:07:20,400
Are you...

181
00:07:20,920 --> 00:07:22,160
worried about me?

182
00:07:25,950 --> 00:07:27,310
Maybe I am worried about a dog?

183
00:07:28,250 --> 00:07:31,350
What if it scratched its leprous skin,
causing it to bleed to death?

184
00:07:32,710 --> 00:07:35,100
You should wait until Dax gets back.

185
00:07:35,120 --> 00:07:36,990
If you got stabbed,

186
00:07:37,060 --> 00:07:39,600
your mother would curse me.

187
00:07:39,620 --> 00:07:40,520
- Fine.
- Alright?

188
00:07:40,540 --> 00:07:42,010
I'll wait until Dax comes back.

189
00:07:42,030 --> 00:07:42,740
Very good.

190
00:07:42,760 --> 00:07:44,150
- Then we'll go together.
- Yeah.

191
00:07:47,510 --> 00:07:49,070
[The D Dorm]

192
00:07:49,200 --> 00:07:49,900
Grandpa,

193
00:07:50,420 --> 00:07:52,530
is this the person who was holding a knife

194
00:07:52,560 --> 00:07:53,430
in Room 407?

195
00:07:57,040 --> 00:07:57,750
Whoa...

196
00:07:59,630 --> 00:08:00,750
I am not sure.

197
00:08:00,990 --> 00:08:02,860
You were a bad person when you were alive.

198
00:08:03,300 --> 00:08:04,420
And now that you're a ghost,

199
00:08:04,440 --> 00:08:06,270
you have bad eyesight, too, huh?

200
00:08:06,790 --> 00:08:08,170
How would I know?

201
00:08:08,190 --> 00:08:11,080
He wore a hood and a face mask.

202
00:08:11,100 --> 00:08:12,970
How would I recognize his face?

203
00:08:12,990 --> 00:08:13,750
So feisty.

204
00:08:13,950 --> 00:08:17,230
I should have let you get stabbed to death.

205
00:08:18,380 --> 00:08:20,390
If I die, I'll still stay by your side.

206
00:08:21,520 --> 00:08:22,790
- Dobby.
- Huh?

207
00:08:23,140 --> 00:08:25,060
Have you talked to
the tenant in Room 407 yet?

208
00:08:25,550 --> 00:08:27,270
So, is he Grandma Gaysorn's grandson?

209
00:08:27,880 --> 00:08:28,970
I haven't talked to him yet.

210
00:08:29,540 --> 00:08:30,380
I already went up there,

211
00:08:30,660 --> 00:08:31,350
but he wasn't home.

212
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:32,789
Why don't we go up there today, then?

213
00:08:33,070 --> 00:08:34,000
He might be home.

214
00:08:34,309 --> 00:08:34,850
Come on.

215
00:08:34,870 --> 00:08:35,710
Don't!

216
00:08:37,390 --> 00:08:38,210
It's too risky.

217
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:52,680
Oh...

218
00:08:54,170 --> 00:08:56,670
What was that about it being risky again?

219
00:08:56,720 --> 00:08:58,000
Oh, I mean...

220
00:08:58,320 --> 00:08:59,470
I don't want you to risk
falling down the stairs.

221
00:08:59,870 --> 00:09:02,410
Do you know how many people
fall down the stairs each year?

222
00:09:02,430 --> 00:09:03,060
- Do you?
- I don't know.

223
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:03,560
What?

224
00:09:03,900 --> 00:09:04,720
And do you?

225
00:09:04,740 --> 00:09:05,680
- You're asking me?
- Mm.

226
00:09:06,670 --> 00:09:07,200
I don't know either.

227
00:09:07,780 --> 00:09:08,690
Then why did you say that?

228
00:09:08,710 --> 00:09:10,470
I just don't want you
to fall down the stairs.

229
00:09:10,580 --> 00:09:12,170
You should work here.

230
00:09:12,560 --> 00:09:14,210
Leave Room 407 to me.

231
00:09:14,230 --> 00:09:15,220
Danis, Danis.

232
00:09:15,240 --> 00:09:15,750
Huh?

233
00:09:15,770 --> 00:09:17,200
Danis, have you seen the news?

234
00:09:17,780 --> 00:09:19,730
Our dorm has a dismemberment case.
[Locals Terrified! Dismemberment Killer Still at Large]

235
00:09:19,750 --> 00:09:20,790
Most importantly,

236
00:09:20,840 --> 00:09:23,470
Dollar said the culprit
is still hiding near our dorm.

237
00:09:23,510 --> 00:09:25,230
Huh? Really?

238
00:09:25,640 --> 00:09:28,970
Is that the killer in Room 407?

239
00:09:29,750 --> 00:09:31,150
Could they be hiding in our dorm?

240
00:09:31,260 --> 00:09:33,190
Exactly...

241
00:09:36,980 --> 00:09:37,650
Whoa...

242
00:09:37,670 --> 00:09:38,740
A dismemberment killer.

243
00:09:38,760 --> 00:09:39,870
That's brutal.

244
00:09:43,230 --> 00:09:43,760
Oops!

245
00:09:43,780 --> 00:09:45,310
Oh... Oh, I'm sorry.

246
00:09:45,770 --> 00:09:46,510
I'm sorry.

247
00:09:52,160 --> 00:09:52,720
Whoa!

248
00:09:54,540 --> 00:09:55,150
You are...

249
00:09:59,110 --> 00:09:59,710
Huh?

250
00:10:00,990 --> 00:10:01,960
I thought I heard Dax.

251
00:10:03,200 --> 00:10:04,270
Was I hearing things?

252
00:10:04,870 --> 00:10:05,900
Ow, ow.

253
00:10:07,390 --> 00:10:08,610
I'm sorry. I really am.

254
00:10:08,630 --> 00:10:11,080
Don't worry, I won't tell anyone

255
00:10:11,100 --> 00:10:11,990
that you are...

256
00:10:15,750 --> 00:10:21,110
♫You cutie pie,
you make me fall so madly in love♫

257
00:10:21,140 --> 00:10:22,750
Ugh, stop it already.

258
00:10:31,640 --> 00:10:34,600
[Disney, occupation: beloved superstar]

259
00:10:34,700 --> 00:10:35,380
Have a seat.

260
00:10:36,160 --> 00:10:36,990
Uh...

261
00:10:37,360 --> 00:10:38,950
Have a seat. Don't be shy.

262
00:10:39,190 --> 00:10:40,230
I'm not shy.

263
00:10:40,960 --> 00:10:41,710
But...

264
00:10:41,940 --> 00:10:42,950
your bed...

265
00:10:43,130 --> 00:10:45,310
reminds me of a series
you've been in before.

266
00:10:46,420 --> 00:10:47,110
"Hia...

267
00:10:47,810 --> 00:10:48,910
Aren't we really going to...

268
00:10:51,530 --> 00:10:52,630
tonight?"

269
00:10:54,390 --> 00:10:55,310
See?

270
00:10:55,360 --> 00:10:57,230
I'm a big fan of yours.

271
00:10:57,250 --> 00:10:59,350
I've seen everything. I know every line.

272
00:10:59,570 --> 00:11:00,360
Thank you.

273
00:11:00,380 --> 00:11:01,830
My name is Dax.

274
00:11:01,850 --> 00:11:03,090
I'm a supporting actor.

275
00:11:03,320 --> 00:11:04,470
Mr. Disney...

276
00:11:04,490 --> 00:11:06,360
you're my superstar, my idol.

277
00:11:06,380 --> 00:11:09,400
I've always dreamed of
being in a series with you.

278
00:11:09,420 --> 00:11:10,650
It can be any series.

279
00:11:11,230 --> 00:11:13,650
I could even play a zombie in 'Zomvivor.'

280
00:11:21,380 --> 00:11:22,390
Is he all there...?

281
00:11:22,840 --> 00:11:23,670
Pardon?

282
00:11:24,230 --> 00:11:25,020
Oh...

283
00:11:25,340 --> 00:11:26,210
I said...

284
00:11:26,230 --> 00:11:29,110
if you get the chance,
please do your best.

285
00:11:29,350 --> 00:11:30,420
Of course I will.

286
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:32,730
By the way...

287
00:11:33,030 --> 00:11:34,670
why are you here?

288
00:11:34,820 --> 00:11:36,310
You're in Room 407, too.

289
00:11:36,550 --> 00:11:37,890
Are you Grandma Gaysorn's relative?

290
00:11:38,690 --> 00:11:40,000
Grandma Gaysorn?

291
00:11:41,190 --> 00:11:43,590
This room is actually my manager's.

292
00:11:44,060 --> 00:11:46,150
But they're at the temple
observing the precepts right now.

293
00:11:46,610 --> 00:11:48,200
When will they be back?

294
00:11:48,750 --> 00:11:50,430
I have to ask them something.

295
00:11:50,860 --> 00:11:52,310
I'm not sure either.

296
00:11:53,400 --> 00:11:57,670
But you have to keep it
a secret that I'm living here.

297
00:11:57,760 --> 00:11:58,970
Not a word to anyone.

298
00:11:58,990 --> 00:12:00,590
I want to keep to myself
and rehearse my script.

299
00:12:00,800 --> 00:12:02,090
I just want some time alone.

300
00:12:03,070 --> 00:12:03,990
Don't tell anyone.

301
00:12:07,710 --> 00:12:09,380
Who says you have to be alone,Your Highness?

302
00:12:10,180 --> 00:12:11,890
I will stay by your side.

303
00:12:14,110 --> 00:12:15,090
See?

304
00:12:15,110 --> 00:12:16,940
I remember every line
from every series you've been in.

305
00:12:19,210 --> 00:12:20,230
To be honest,

306
00:12:20,290 --> 00:12:23,550
I'm not a fan of the actor
who played the royal guard.

307
00:12:23,930 --> 00:12:26,350
I think he tried
a bit too hard to look cool.

308
00:12:27,230 --> 00:12:28,630
If he's as handsome as I am,
that's another story.

309
00:12:28,960 --> 00:12:29,710
Huh?

310
00:12:31,710 --> 00:12:32,730
So...

311
00:12:33,110 --> 00:12:35,010
you promise to keep this a secret, right?

312
00:12:35,190 --> 00:12:35,980
I promise!

313
00:12:37,840 --> 00:12:40,720
[DO-MUN-DRIP]

314
00:12:44,970 --> 00:12:45,960
Wow...

315
00:12:45,980 --> 00:12:49,070
The mangoes from the farm
your mother owns are amazing.

316
00:12:49,130 --> 00:12:50,960
What type of mango is this? It's so nutty.

317
00:12:50,980 --> 00:12:51,830
Over 1,000 Thai baht.

318
00:12:52,490 --> 00:12:53,110
Ugh...

319
00:12:53,470 --> 00:12:54,400
He's asking about the type.

320
00:12:54,420 --> 00:12:55,640
- The type?
- Yeah.

321
00:12:55,670 --> 00:12:57,590
- I thought he asked about the price.
- No.

322
00:12:57,610 --> 00:12:58,470
Tell him, tell him.

323
00:12:58,490 --> 00:13:00,270
It'd be too easy to just tell you.

324
00:13:00,290 --> 00:13:01,340
Let's play a game.

325
00:13:01,360 --> 00:13:02,550
I'll give you a hint.

326
00:13:02,570 --> 00:13:04,890
If you can guess correctly,
I'll give you two mangoes.

327
00:13:05,130 --> 00:13:06,140
- Okay.
- Are you in?

328
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:06,990
Yes, yes, yes.

329
00:13:07,010 --> 00:13:08,910
Here's a hint about

330
00:13:08,930 --> 00:13:10,110
the mango you're eating...

331
00:13:10,340 --> 00:13:11,830
Sky Boom-Boom.

332
00:13:12,160 --> 00:13:13,220
It's...

333
00:13:13,870 --> 00:13:15,190
Lightning mango!

334
00:13:16,570 --> 00:13:17,430
What even is that?

335
00:13:17,450 --> 00:13:19,390
There's no such mango variety, alright?

336
00:13:19,630 --> 00:13:20,360
Try again!

337
00:13:20,380 --> 00:13:21,790
Sky Boom-Boom.

338
00:13:24,120 --> 00:13:24,670
Oh.

339
00:13:24,690 --> 00:13:25,950
Falan mango, thunderous sky in Thai!

340
00:13:25,970 --> 00:13:26,540
Correct!

341
00:13:26,560 --> 00:13:27,160
- Whoa.
- Oh.

342
00:13:27,180 --> 00:13:28,230
You got one right.

343
00:13:28,250 --> 00:13:30,490
What about these fibrous ones?

344
00:13:30,510 --> 00:13:31,070
That's plywood.

345
00:13:32,010 --> 00:13:32,720
Mangoes!

346
00:13:32,740 --> 00:13:34,510
- Plywood is made from wood fibers, though.
- No, no.

347
00:13:34,550 --> 00:13:35,830
- That one?
- Yes, yes.

348
00:13:35,890 --> 00:13:36,830
Here's a hint.

349
00:13:38,700 --> 00:13:39,230
Ooh...

350
00:13:39,450 --> 00:13:40,030
Oh?

351
00:13:40,260 --> 00:13:40,880
Captured?

352
00:13:41,910 --> 00:13:43,200
What do you mean, captured?

353
00:13:43,220 --> 00:13:44,150
Did the mango commit tax fraud?

354
00:13:44,670 --> 00:13:46,270
No. Watch again.

355
00:13:50,560 --> 00:13:51,760
Ooh!

356
00:13:52,390 --> 00:13:53,510
Sexy mango.

357
00:13:53,890 --> 00:13:54,610
Sexy mango.

358
00:13:54,630 --> 00:13:56,160
I've never had that before.

359
00:13:56,180 --> 00:13:57,030
We don't even have that.

360
00:13:57,230 --> 00:13:57,870
What?

361
00:13:58,050 --> 00:13:58,960
Watch closely.

362
00:14:02,790 --> 00:14:03,760
Ooh...

363
00:14:04,290 --> 00:14:05,710
With this squeeze...

364
00:14:05,900 --> 00:14:06,860
it has to be...

365
00:14:07,070 --> 00:14:08,110
Okrong mango, cleavage in Thai!

366
00:14:08,130 --> 00:14:09,490
- There!
- Good job!

367
00:14:09,510 --> 00:14:10,960
You got two right.

368
00:14:11,070 --> 00:14:14,230
What about this nutty,
crisp, and sour one?

369
00:14:14,250 --> 00:14:15,670
Hey handsome,

370
00:14:15,910 --> 00:14:16,830
wanna...

371
00:14:17,400 --> 00:14:18,950
have a one-night stand with me?

372
00:14:18,990 --> 00:14:19,750
Okay.

373
00:14:19,870 --> 00:14:20,540
- I'll go.
- Let's go.

374
00:14:20,560 --> 00:14:21,850
- No, you're guessing the mango!
- Oh, no?

375
00:14:21,870 --> 00:14:23,250
- Guess the mango.
- I see.

376
00:14:24,500 --> 00:14:25,430
Handsome...

377
00:14:26,130 --> 00:14:27,110
This seductive...

378
00:14:28,600 --> 00:14:31,080
- Are you still thinking?
- I am, I am.

379
00:14:32,780 --> 00:14:33,750
Rad mango, seductive ladies in Thai!

380
00:14:33,900 --> 00:14:34,630
That's right!

381
00:14:35,700 --> 00:14:36,990
- Good job!
- What's Rad mango in English?

382
00:14:37,020 --> 00:14:37,550
In English?

383
00:14:37,570 --> 00:14:38,540
Char-rad-e mango.

384
00:14:38,560 --> 00:14:39,390
- Huh?!
- Whoa?!

385
00:14:40,050 --> 00:14:41,350
- Take this.
- Ow!

386
00:14:41,390 --> 00:14:43,060
You're a pro, huh?

387
00:14:43,360 --> 00:14:45,150
I'm gonna send you
to live with Mom at the farm.

388
00:14:45,170 --> 00:14:46,020
I'm not going.

389
00:14:46,250 --> 00:14:48,630
Just so I can go back and hear them
whisper that Mom only took me in?

390
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:51,400
You and Mom look alike,
but I look nothing like her.

391
00:14:53,930 --> 00:14:55,070
Aw...

392
00:14:55,090 --> 00:14:56,750
You may not look like her,

393
00:14:57,110 --> 00:14:58,630
but you look like Dad.

394
00:14:59,200 --> 00:15:00,260
Bulky,

395
00:15:00,360 --> 00:15:01,370
big and tall,

396
00:15:01,630 --> 00:15:03,850
with lots of muscle.

397
00:15:03,870 --> 00:15:05,510
I only see fat. Not muscle.

398
00:15:06,650 --> 00:15:07,270
He has muscle.

399
00:15:07,660 --> 00:15:08,670
It's just a bit hidden.

400
00:15:08,860 --> 00:15:10,110
Like inverted nipples.

401
00:15:10,130 --> 00:15:11,710
It's still there; you just can't see it.

402
00:15:11,730 --> 00:15:12,830
They fold inward...

403
00:15:12,850 --> 00:15:14,550
Don't explain anymore. It's disgusting.

404
00:15:14,570 --> 00:15:15,010
Really?

405
00:15:15,030 --> 00:15:16,510
You're comparing it to nipples?
Are you crazy?

406
00:15:16,530 --> 00:15:17,380
Whoa...

407
00:15:17,540 --> 00:15:18,790
- Uh, Dolly?
- Yes?

408
00:15:18,810 --> 00:15:20,050
The coffee is ready.

409
00:15:20,070 --> 00:15:21,310
Please deliver it for me.

410
00:15:22,200 --> 00:15:24,220
Rest assured, I'll take care of it.

411
00:15:24,690 --> 00:15:26,230
Mr. Drip's café is like my own.

412
00:15:26,600 --> 00:15:27,230
Huh?

413
00:15:28,100 --> 00:15:28,910
What do you mean, "Huh?"

414
00:15:29,380 --> 00:15:30,070
Well...

415
00:15:30,160 --> 00:15:32,030
we're neighbors.

416
00:15:32,130 --> 00:15:32,950
We should help each other out.

417
00:15:32,980 --> 00:15:34,290
Well, well, well...

418
00:15:34,310 --> 00:15:37,250
When Auntie Duang asks you
to deliver food, you always drag your feet.

419
00:15:37,280 --> 00:15:38,430
But now, look how eager you are.

420
00:15:38,930 --> 00:15:39,990
Come on, now.

421
00:15:40,250 --> 00:15:41,160
I'll get going.

422
00:15:41,180 --> 00:15:42,430
We can talk about the mangoes later.

423
00:15:42,810 --> 00:15:43,340
Oh, Dolly.

424
00:15:43,360 --> 00:15:44,430
Oh, Dawin.

425
00:15:46,390 --> 00:15:47,380
Oh, hey, Mr. Dawin.

426
00:15:47,530 --> 00:15:48,810
You're here for the mangoes, right?

427
00:15:48,830 --> 00:15:50,870
- That's right.
- I've got that ready for you over there.

428
00:15:50,890 --> 00:15:52,190
- Thank you.
- My pleasure.

429
00:15:55,170 --> 00:15:56,670
Where's my chili salt dip?

430
00:15:56,810 --> 00:15:58,110
Oh...

431
00:15:58,510 --> 00:15:59,730
darn it, Mom.

432
00:15:59,750 --> 00:16:02,110
At her age, she often forgets things.

433
00:16:02,170 --> 00:16:03,170
She probably forgot to make some for you.

434
00:16:03,190 --> 00:16:03,670
It's alright.

435
00:16:03,690 --> 00:16:05,910
Daeng, give him some of ours.

436
00:16:09,640 --> 00:16:10,550
No way.

437
00:16:10,870 --> 00:16:11,790
It's mine.

438
00:16:11,900 --> 00:16:13,830
He's our mom's customer. Be nice.

439
00:16:14,910 --> 00:16:16,200
Don't be difficult.

440
00:16:16,220 --> 00:16:17,300
Share a little, will you?

441
00:16:18,650 --> 00:16:19,880
May I have a cup?

442
00:16:19,900 --> 00:16:20,830
Oh, of course.

443
00:16:22,270 --> 00:16:22,940
Here.

444
00:16:23,610 --> 00:16:24,270
Share some.

445
00:16:24,430 --> 00:16:25,190
Pour it in.

446
00:16:25,210 --> 00:16:26,360
Ugh, we've got plenty.

447
00:16:26,380 --> 00:16:27,350
This is enough.

448
00:16:28,050 --> 00:16:29,430
Hey, why so stingy?

449
00:16:31,540 --> 00:16:32,420
- Whoa!
- Ow!

450
00:16:34,070 --> 00:16:35,470
My eyes!

451
00:16:35,490 --> 00:16:37,030
Whoa, I'm sorry. I didn't mean to.

452
00:16:37,070 --> 00:16:39,070
- Tissues, tissues.
- Ow, my eyes!

453
00:16:39,110 --> 00:16:40,590
I can't take it anymore.

454
00:16:40,630 --> 00:16:41,150
Where is it?

455
00:16:41,170 --> 00:16:42,160
Hey, are you okay?

456
00:16:42,810 --> 00:16:45,060
- Ugh, he's over there!
- Oh, whoa!

457
00:16:45,180 --> 00:16:46,510
Hey, go check on him.

458
00:16:46,670 --> 00:16:47,610
Oh!

459
00:16:47,630 --> 00:16:48,510
Don't crowd around him.

460
00:16:48,870 --> 00:16:49,650
Give him some space!

461
00:16:49,670 --> 00:16:51,150
- There's no one there.
- Gently, gently.

462
00:16:51,550 --> 00:16:52,910
- Ow.
- Get him to a doctor.

463
00:16:52,960 --> 00:16:54,010
- Doctor, doctor.
- Go, go, go!

464
00:16:54,030 --> 00:16:55,680
- Go see a doctor.
- Come on, go.

465
00:16:55,700 --> 00:16:56,170
Go, go, go.

466
00:16:56,190 --> 00:16:58,060
- Help. I can't see.
- Alright, go, go.

467
00:16:58,080 --> 00:16:59,580
- Ow.
- Let's go, let's go.

468
00:17:00,270 --> 00:17:02,230
We're in the same line of work.

469
00:17:02,250 --> 00:17:04,869
I know that when you have to
memorize your lines or...

470
00:17:05,180 --> 00:17:07,310
get into character,
you need to concentrate.

471
00:17:07,990 --> 00:17:08,750
By the way...

472
00:17:08,890 --> 00:17:11,470
What movie are you rehearsing for right now?

473
00:17:11,829 --> 00:17:13,359
I can be your acting partner.

474
00:17:14,069 --> 00:17:15,430
Whether you need a som tum vendor...

475
00:17:17,069 --> 00:17:18,230
Delish som tum

476
00:17:18,430 --> 00:17:20,310
right this way!

477
00:17:20,329 --> 00:17:21,310
This way!

478
00:17:21,410 --> 00:17:22,390
Or a cop.

479
00:17:23,810 --> 00:17:24,510
Drop your weapon.

480
00:17:24,970 --> 00:17:25,829
Put your hands up.

481
00:17:27,910 --> 00:17:29,110
Or maybe a midwife.

482
00:17:34,190 --> 00:17:35,270
Push, Nak.

483
00:17:39,790 --> 00:17:40,590
Mak,

484
00:17:40,610 --> 00:17:42,230
help me...

485
00:17:43,060 --> 00:17:43,990
Ugh!

486
00:17:44,100 --> 00:17:45,190
You can stop now.

487
00:17:45,980 --> 00:17:47,390
If you really want to help me out,

488
00:17:47,490 --> 00:17:48,160
go.

489
00:17:48,950 --> 00:17:51,350
Lie down and stay still, like a dead body.

490
00:17:52,960 --> 00:17:53,590
Huh?

491
00:18:00,420 --> 00:18:01,360
Go, go.

492
00:18:01,810 --> 00:18:03,320
- No, not that. No.
- Huh?

493
00:18:03,340 --> 00:18:03,850
What do you mean, no?

494
00:18:03,870 --> 00:18:05,410
That isn't a white cane,
that's my baton.

495
00:18:05,430 --> 00:18:06,190
Your cane is here.

496
00:18:06,830 --> 00:18:07,830
Stop knocking on it already.

497
00:18:08,560 --> 00:18:09,130
This way.

498
00:18:09,150 --> 00:18:09,870
Careful.

499
00:18:11,770 --> 00:18:14,560
With his customer getting blinded like this,

500
00:18:14,710 --> 00:18:17,540
has Mr. Drip even checked
the feng shui of his cafe?

501
00:18:17,560 --> 00:18:18,580
I'm not blind yet.

502
00:18:19,610 --> 00:18:20,270
This way.

503
00:18:20,970 --> 00:18:22,070
Who talks to coffee beans?

504
00:18:23,250 --> 00:18:24,160
I'm not blind yet.

505
00:18:24,510 --> 00:18:25,790
The doctor said my eyes are inflamed,

506
00:18:25,810 --> 00:18:27,430
so I have to wear eye shields temporarily.

507
00:18:29,730 --> 00:18:33,790
Poor thing...

508
00:18:33,900 --> 00:18:35,470
Even if you're not blind,
it's practically the same thing.

509
00:18:35,590 --> 00:18:38,690
Someone who once lived in a world of light

510
00:18:38,710 --> 00:18:40,030
now has to live in darkness.

511
00:18:40,590 --> 00:18:42,230
Even walking has become difficult.

512
00:18:42,310 --> 00:18:45,190
Oh, and your room is on the fourth floor...

513
00:18:45,210 --> 00:18:47,110
You poor soul.

514
00:18:48,580 --> 00:18:50,830
I'll just chalk it up
to my own bad luck, Guard Dum.

515
00:18:50,990 --> 00:18:51,610
Yes...

516
00:18:52,130 --> 00:18:53,390
Thank you for worrying about me.

517
00:18:53,410 --> 00:18:55,150
It's alright. I hope you get well soon.

518
00:18:55,710 --> 00:18:57,050
No, he's that way.

519
00:18:58,330 --> 00:18:59,200
This way. Here.

520
00:18:59,220 --> 00:18:59,550
Ugh.

521
00:18:59,570 --> 00:19:00,990
If you can't see, just stay still.

522
00:19:01,250 --> 00:19:04,030
If it's that difficult,
why not go back to the hospital?

523
00:19:06,470 --> 00:19:08,510
I can't afford a hospital room.

524
00:19:08,670 --> 00:19:09,380
Ugh.

525
00:19:09,570 --> 00:19:10,550
There's no need for him to do that.

526
00:19:10,670 --> 00:19:11,710
You have to take care of him.

527
00:19:11,750 --> 00:19:12,260
Huh?

528
00:19:12,300 --> 00:19:13,830
What are you confused about?
You hurt his eyes.

529
00:19:13,850 --> 00:19:14,710
You have to take responsibility.

530
00:19:15,310 --> 00:19:17,110
Listen, from now on...

531
00:19:17,690 --> 00:19:20,350
you have to be his eyes
until he recovers.

532
00:19:21,110 --> 00:19:22,070
No way!

533
00:19:23,190 --> 00:19:24,030
I got chills.

534
00:19:24,490 --> 00:19:26,030
If I have to take care of him,

535
00:19:26,180 --> 00:19:28,070
I'd rather hire a caregiver.

536
00:19:29,370 --> 00:19:30,310
Your medicine is right here.

537
00:19:30,330 --> 00:19:30,830
What?

538
00:19:30,850 --> 00:19:32,190
Hey, that's a waste of money.

539
00:19:33,510 --> 00:19:34,430
He's blind, though.

540
00:19:37,360 --> 00:19:38,570
- Guard Dum!
- Oh...

541
00:19:38,590 --> 00:19:41,190
I thought you said this would make
your brother hold my hand?

542
00:19:42,160 --> 00:19:42,830
Huh?

543
00:19:42,850 --> 00:19:44,590
Mr. Dawin, you can see?

544
00:19:46,310 --> 00:19:47,550
Don't tell Handyman Daeng about this.

545
00:19:47,570 --> 00:19:49,580
I just wanted an excuse to hold his hand

546
00:19:49,750 --> 00:19:51,030
and talk to Gramps' ghost.

547
00:19:51,330 --> 00:19:52,290
Don't tell anyone.

548
00:19:52,310 --> 00:19:53,070
What now?

549
00:19:54,160 --> 00:19:55,750
I forgot how heartless he can be.

550
00:19:58,620 --> 00:19:59,620
No wonder...

551
00:19:59,910 --> 00:20:01,580
he kept pushing us together.

552
00:20:02,150 --> 00:20:04,670
This time...you won't just see ghosts.

553
00:20:04,960 --> 00:20:07,130
You'll come face-to-face
with the Grim Reaper.

554
00:20:13,530 --> 00:20:14,560
Let me check the number real quick...

555
00:20:14,890 --> 00:20:15,590
It's the right one, though.

556
00:20:18,450 --> 00:20:19,230
- What?
- Huh?

557
00:20:19,980 --> 00:20:23,620
Room 407's listed number
isn't going through.

558
00:20:23,930 --> 00:20:24,970
Did he put in a fake number?

559
00:20:24,990 --> 00:20:26,070
How would I know?

560
00:20:27,180 --> 00:20:27,980
Ms. Danis!

561
00:20:28,540 --> 00:20:29,250
Ms. Danis?

562
00:20:29,270 --> 00:20:31,110
Dennis isn't around. She stepped out.

563
00:20:31,170 --> 00:20:32,100
Is something up?

564
00:20:32,260 --> 00:20:32,890
Where did she go?

565
00:20:32,910 --> 00:20:33,230
Oh!

566
00:20:33,250 --> 00:20:33,760
Oh!

567
00:20:34,410 --> 00:20:36,160
Are you dressing up as
an oil-seeping pillar?

568
00:20:36,660 --> 00:20:37,340
Both yantra cloth

569
00:20:37,360 --> 00:20:38,410
and three-colored cloth.

570
00:20:39,030 --> 00:20:39,910
Auntie Duang, what are you doing?

571
00:20:39,930 --> 00:20:41,160
I'm not dressing up as anything.

572
00:20:41,180 --> 00:20:42,870
These are sacred items.

573
00:20:43,710 --> 00:20:45,360
Dollar told me

574
00:20:45,380 --> 00:20:48,140
the killer is still
lurking around this dorm,

575
00:20:48,160 --> 00:20:49,030
so I'm keeping these close

576
00:20:49,230 --> 00:20:50,750
for protection.

577
00:20:51,910 --> 00:20:53,330
If I were the killer,

578
00:20:53,350 --> 00:20:55,640
I would not approach her.

579
00:20:55,660 --> 00:20:57,190
She is definitely crazy.

580
00:20:57,950 --> 00:20:58,800
- Oh.
- Hm?

581
00:20:58,820 --> 00:21:00,710
Have you talked to
the tenant in Room 407 yet?

582
00:21:00,820 --> 00:21:02,100
I haven't, Auntie Duang.

583
00:21:02,190 --> 00:21:04,170
I'm waiting for Dax so we can go together.

584
00:21:04,190 --> 00:21:05,250
Want me to take you there?

585
00:21:05,270 --> 00:21:06,270
I think he's home.

586
00:21:06,510 --> 00:21:08,540
He called me to order food
this morning.

587
00:21:08,560 --> 00:21:10,410
I left the food at his door.

588
00:21:10,710 --> 00:21:12,110
You can try your luck.

589
00:21:12,160 --> 00:21:13,510
One crazy person versus another.

590
00:21:13,710 --> 00:21:15,310
They might just balance each other out.

591
00:21:16,390 --> 00:21:16,960
Let's go.

592
00:21:17,270 --> 00:21:18,140
It's alright, Auntie Duang.

593
00:21:18,290 --> 00:21:19,110
I'll handle it.

594
00:21:19,130 --> 00:21:20,840
Mom, Mom. Mom!

595
00:21:20,860 --> 00:21:22,020
- Ugh, Dolly,
- Mom!

596
00:21:22,040 --> 00:21:23,180
why are you making a fuss?!

597
00:21:23,200 --> 00:21:24,050
This is bad, Mom!

598
00:21:24,070 --> 00:21:26,070
Dollar sent me a photo of the killer.

599
00:21:26,090 --> 00:21:27,120
Really? Where?

600
00:21:27,140 --> 00:21:27,710
Here.

601
00:21:27,800 --> 00:21:28,310
Oh?

602
00:21:31,120 --> 00:21:32,700
Crunchy boy is the killer?

603
00:21:34,570 --> 00:21:35,950
Wrong one. Not this one.

604
00:21:38,720 --> 00:21:39,540
Whoa...

605
00:21:39,560 --> 00:21:41,070
Why do you have
so many photos of the crunchy boy?

606
00:21:41,690 --> 00:21:43,090
- Uh...
- For the ordination hall walls?

607
00:21:43,880 --> 00:21:45,770
These are just references for my costumes.

608
00:21:45,790 --> 00:21:46,670
Yeah, yeah.

609
00:21:46,870 --> 00:21:47,750
Come on, let me see.

610
00:21:47,780 --> 00:21:48,750
Here.

611
00:21:48,820 --> 00:21:49,710
This is the real killer.

612
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:50,560
Oh?

613
00:21:50,580 --> 00:21:52,470
He looks just like
the tenant from Room 407.

614
00:21:52,580 --> 00:21:54,190
Right? I feel like
I've seen him before, too.

615
00:21:54,490 --> 00:21:55,250
No, not really.

616
00:21:55,270 --> 00:21:58,070
That is him.
The bag looks just like his.

617
00:21:59,300 --> 00:21:59,710
Oh.

618
00:22:01,050 --> 00:22:01,820
Dax texted me.

619
00:22:01,840 --> 00:22:02,340
Huh?

620
00:22:02,640 --> 00:22:05,340
Dobby, I'm with the tenant from Room 407.

621
00:22:05,610 --> 00:22:07,990
"Don't worry, I'll handle it."

622
00:22:08,170 --> 00:22:09,050
- Huh?!
- Huh?!

623
00:22:09,380 --> 00:22:11,150
Is Mr. Dax in the room with the killer?

624
00:22:11,180 --> 00:22:11,800
Oh, no...

625
00:22:12,220 --> 00:22:13,510
Dobby, call him.

626
00:22:13,700 --> 00:22:14,970
Tell him to run. Hurry!

627
00:22:16,720 --> 00:22:18,110
I put my phone on airplane mode,
like you asked.

628
00:22:19,050 --> 00:22:20,930
That way, no one will interrupt us

629
00:22:20,950 --> 00:22:22,070
while we're rehearsing.

630
00:22:27,880 --> 00:22:28,620
Can you reach him?

631
00:22:28,640 --> 00:22:29,490
He's not answering.

632
00:22:30,200 --> 00:22:31,110
He turned his phone off.

633
00:22:31,130 --> 00:22:32,310
Maybe he's in danger.

634
00:22:34,280 --> 00:22:34,830
How about this?

635
00:22:34,870 --> 00:22:37,560
Dolly, tell Dollar to bring
the police here right now.

636
00:22:37,580 --> 00:22:38,990
- Right now, come on.
- Hey!

637
00:22:39,380 --> 00:22:41,470
Dax will be dead
before the police show up.

638
00:22:41,490 --> 00:22:42,110
Yeah.

639
00:22:42,690 --> 00:22:43,980
Then I'll go help him.

640
00:22:44,000 --> 00:22:44,710
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

641
00:22:44,730 --> 00:22:46,060
Bring the police up
the second they get here.

642
00:22:46,080 --> 00:22:46,640
Okay.

643
00:22:46,660 --> 00:22:47,470
- Alright.
- Hurry.

644
00:22:47,620 --> 00:22:48,070
Hey.

645
00:22:48,520 --> 00:22:49,590
Hurry up!

646
00:22:51,930 --> 00:22:53,320
Oh, you're here already?

647
00:22:53,730 --> 00:22:54,940
What you did was wrong.

648
00:22:54,960 --> 00:22:57,940
You can't hire someone else
to take care of Mr. Dawin.

649
00:22:57,990 --> 00:23:00,250
You hurt him, so you have to
take care of him yourself.

650
00:23:00,270 --> 00:23:01,980
You can't trust anyone these days.

651
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:04,190
What if they stab Mr. Dawin
when you're not around?

652
00:23:04,230 --> 00:23:05,200
Stabby-stab.

653
00:23:05,220 --> 00:23:05,630
What will you do?

654
00:23:05,650 --> 00:23:06,590
What if they have a gun?

655
00:23:06,610 --> 00:23:08,230
He'll get shot. Bang, bang, bang.

656
00:23:08,290 --> 00:23:09,350
What if there's a knife
attached to the gun?

657
00:23:09,720 --> 00:23:10,250
Stab.

658
00:23:10,270 --> 00:23:10,870
Bang!

659
00:23:10,920 --> 00:23:11,310
Stab.

660
00:23:11,350 --> 00:23:11,870
Bang!

661
00:23:11,890 --> 00:23:12,350
Stab.

662
00:23:12,370 --> 00:23:12,830
Bang!

663
00:23:12,850 --> 00:23:13,120
Stab.

664
00:23:13,140 --> 00:23:14,270
- Ugh!
- Ugh!

665
00:23:14,310 --> 00:23:16,070
He's like Swiss cheese at this point.
Put this away.

666
00:23:16,990 --> 00:23:17,940
Right in the eye!

667
00:23:19,020 --> 00:23:20,830
If you're going to hire someone
to take care of me,

668
00:23:21,170 --> 00:23:22,070
I'll have to turn that down.

669
00:23:22,170 --> 00:23:23,610
I'm not comfortable with strangers.

670
00:23:23,630 --> 00:23:24,990
I'll take care of you.

671
00:23:26,350 --> 00:23:27,370
You sure change your mind fast.

672
00:23:27,590 --> 00:23:30,550
When I stepped outside, I realized

673
00:23:30,580 --> 00:23:33,470
I'd injured Mr. Dawin,

674
00:23:34,490 --> 00:23:37,150
so I thought it was best
to take responsibility.

675
00:23:37,830 --> 00:23:40,430
To prove that to you,

676
00:23:40,450 --> 00:23:43,070
I bought these steamed buns for you.

677
00:23:45,350 --> 00:23:45,880
Ow.

678
00:23:45,900 --> 00:23:48,380
Hot, hot, hot!

679
00:23:48,430 --> 00:23:49,550
It's hot.

680
00:23:50,220 --> 00:23:52,430
Po, shush.

681
00:23:52,550 --> 00:23:56,950
Didn't I say I'd take care of Mr. Dawin?

682
00:24:00,800 --> 00:24:02,750
The steamed bun is still hot, though.

683
00:24:02,870 --> 00:24:04,930
Let me cool it down first.

684
00:24:08,390 --> 00:24:09,710
Whoa...

685
00:24:10,820 --> 00:24:12,510
Alright,

686
00:24:12,710 --> 00:24:13,350
It's not as hot now.

687
00:24:13,510 --> 00:24:14,110
Go on.

688
00:24:14,420 --> 00:24:15,230
Mr. Dawin,

689
00:24:15,310 --> 00:24:16,830
open wide. I'll feed you.

690
00:24:18,150 --> 00:24:20,150
I'm...not hungry yet.

691
00:24:22,100 --> 00:24:22,990
What?

692
00:24:23,100 --> 00:24:25,020
This is just a small steamed bun.

693
00:24:25,040 --> 00:24:27,750
Or maybe you don't want me
to take care of you anymore?

694
00:24:30,300 --> 00:24:31,580
Uh...

695
00:24:32,220 --> 00:24:33,310
I'll eat it myself.

696
00:24:34,310 --> 00:24:36,910
It's a little embarrassing
having you feed me.

697
00:24:37,020 --> 00:24:38,390
Oh...

698
00:24:38,700 --> 00:24:39,590
Alright, then.

699
00:24:42,090 --> 00:24:43,030
Oh...

700
00:24:43,290 --> 00:24:43,990
Uh...

701
00:24:44,350 --> 00:24:45,270
Oops!

702
00:24:45,320 --> 00:24:46,020
Oh...

703
00:24:46,320 --> 00:24:47,300
I'm sorry.

704
00:24:47,820 --> 00:24:49,270
I dropped it.

705
00:24:49,290 --> 00:24:51,270
- Oh, such a shame.
- Oh.

706
00:24:51,690 --> 00:24:52,950
He can't eat it anymore.

707
00:24:53,040 --> 00:24:53,870
It's okay.

708
00:24:54,560 --> 00:24:56,300
I'll get you a new one.

709
00:24:56,490 --> 00:24:57,190
Phew...

710
00:25:07,790 --> 00:25:08,630
Oh, wow...

711
00:25:11,320 --> 00:25:12,230
So cruel.

712
00:25:19,480 --> 00:25:20,180
It's not hot anymore.

713
00:25:20,200 --> 00:25:20,960
Hey...

714
00:25:20,980 --> 00:25:22,350
Alright, open wide.

715
00:25:23,120 --> 00:25:24,390
Uh... Okay.

716
00:25:32,490 --> 00:25:34,030
He only had to fake
an eye infection at first.

717
00:25:34,190 --> 00:25:36,950
But at this rate,
he'll be fighting demons on the toilet.

718
00:25:38,870 --> 00:25:41,430
I think Daeng already
knows we lied to him.

719
00:25:41,780 --> 00:25:43,150
- Let's make a run for it.
- Yeah.

720
00:25:43,900 --> 00:25:45,510
Where do you think you're going, Po?

721
00:25:46,730 --> 00:25:49,290
Stay and help me
coax Mr. Dawin into eating first.

722
00:25:50,350 --> 00:25:53,550
He seems suspicious of me whenever
I try to take care of him, right?

723
00:25:54,480 --> 00:25:54,920
Uh...

724
00:25:56,170 --> 00:25:59,310
Then I suppose
I can't take care of you anymore.

725
00:26:01,540 --> 00:26:02,190
Wait!

726
00:26:03,460 --> 00:26:05,670
I'm not suspicious of you
taking care of me at all.

727
00:26:09,570 --> 00:26:10,790
Then eat.

728
00:26:14,860 --> 00:26:17,270
No one will ever find out
that I'm the killer.

729
00:26:18,390 --> 00:26:20,910
You'll take this secret to your grave.

730
00:26:24,280 --> 00:26:24,910
Wait.

731
00:26:25,760 --> 00:26:28,150
This line in the script is too short.

732
00:26:28,460 --> 00:26:31,430
I can't quite tell what kind of fear
this character is experiencing.

733
00:26:31,600 --> 00:26:32,950
Ugh...

734
00:26:33,320 --> 00:26:35,020
You can act however you want.

735
00:26:35,040 --> 00:26:36,910
You'll die after one stab anyway.

736
00:26:37,860 --> 00:26:38,590
That won't do.

737
00:26:39,200 --> 00:26:41,200
We need to understand
the character's emotions

738
00:26:41,220 --> 00:26:42,990
to know how to portray them.

739
00:26:43,100 --> 00:26:44,110
Maybe he's really scared.

740
00:26:44,180 --> 00:26:47,390
No. Hey...don't come any closer.

741
00:26:47,750 --> 00:26:49,710
Or maybe it's resentment.

742
00:26:50,780 --> 00:26:52,190
If you kill me...

743
00:26:52,540 --> 00:26:54,750
I'll come back as a ghost
and break your neck.

744
00:26:56,230 --> 00:26:57,990
Or is it Uno Laothong's fear?

745
00:26:58,680 --> 00:27:01,700
I can't. I can't with this house.
It's too scary.

746
00:27:02,350 --> 00:27:04,320
I don't want to be here any longer.

747
00:27:04,340 --> 00:27:05,310
I don't want to be here either...

748
00:27:05,960 --> 00:27:06,660
Pardon?

749
00:27:06,960 --> 00:27:07,640
Oh.

750
00:27:08,160 --> 00:27:09,040
I think...

751
00:27:09,580 --> 00:27:10,630
we should move on to the next scene.

752
00:27:10,680 --> 00:27:12,110
Let's move on from being threatened...

753
00:27:12,270 --> 00:27:13,390
to the chase scene.

754
00:27:13,790 --> 00:27:15,110
Let's go full send.

755
00:27:15,140 --> 00:27:15,910
By the way...

756
00:27:16,270 --> 00:27:17,830
how would he be feeling as he runs away?

757
00:27:18,090 --> 00:27:18,710
Huh?

758
00:27:20,880 --> 00:27:22,230
Is he running away in fear?

759
00:27:26,080 --> 00:27:27,950
Or is he paranoid?

760
00:27:29,240 --> 00:27:30,320
Don't follow me.

761
00:27:31,290 --> 00:27:32,270
Don't follow me!

762
00:27:34,550 --> 00:27:36,510
Or maybe like Toon Artiwara.

763
00:27:37,470 --> 00:27:39,510
I want Thai people to be healthy!

764
00:27:41,620 --> 00:27:42,350
Which is it?

765
00:27:42,740 --> 00:27:44,070
Run however you want.

766
00:27:44,240 --> 00:27:45,120
Just run.

767
00:27:45,560 --> 00:27:47,210
Run out of the room. Go on.

768
00:27:47,230 --> 00:27:47,990
Run.

769
00:27:48,720 --> 00:27:49,700
Don't kill me!

770
00:27:49,720 --> 00:27:50,990
Don't... Don't kill me.

771
00:27:51,100 --> 00:27:53,350
Don't kill me!

772
00:27:53,670 --> 00:27:54,630
Don't kill me...

773
00:27:54,710 --> 00:27:56,190
Ugh...

774
00:27:56,490 --> 00:27:57,750
Just kill me already.

775
00:27:58,510 --> 00:28:00,550
[The D Dorm]

776
00:28:04,520 --> 00:28:05,640
Do not tell me...

777
00:28:05,820 --> 00:28:07,710
Dax is dead dead?

778
00:28:09,300 --> 00:28:10,550
How could you say that?

779
00:28:10,700 --> 00:28:11,960
That's my friend, Grandpa.

780
00:28:14,490 --> 00:28:15,690
I'm here to help.

781
00:28:16,990 --> 00:28:17,990
Oh?

782
00:28:19,160 --> 00:28:20,830
What are you wearing, Mr. Dolly?

783
00:28:21,460 --> 00:28:22,600
I wanted to help,

784
00:28:22,620 --> 00:28:23,490
but Mom was worried about me,

785
00:28:23,510 --> 00:28:25,510
so she made me wear
these things for protection.

786
00:28:26,310 --> 00:28:27,320
Come on, now...

787
00:28:27,690 --> 00:28:28,520
Here!

788
00:28:29,120 --> 00:28:30,630
Mom told me to give you this.

789
00:28:30,960 --> 00:28:31,940
For me?

790
00:28:36,090 --> 00:28:37,040
What?

791
00:28:47,710 --> 00:28:48,670
Dax.

792
00:28:48,950 --> 00:28:50,160
Whoa...

793
00:28:56,750 --> 00:28:57,310
Oh!

794
00:28:58,220 --> 00:29:01,510
Dax is dead dead!

795
00:29:02,340 --> 00:29:03,350
Dax...

796
00:29:06,040 --> 00:29:07,790
It's gonna be okay, Mr. Dobby.

797
00:29:07,940 --> 00:29:08,680
Wow.

798
00:29:08,700 --> 00:29:10,150
That was amazing, Mr. Disney.

799
00:29:10,460 --> 00:29:13,290
The moment you checked to see
if I was still breathing...

800
00:29:13,500 --> 00:29:14,060
Wow...

801
00:29:14,080 --> 00:29:16,160
Your eyes and that grin make you look like

802
00:29:16,580 --> 00:29:18,610
a killer who's actually trying to murder me.

803
00:29:18,630 --> 00:29:20,720
If I wanted to kill you,
I would've done it the moment you said...

804
00:29:20,740 --> 00:29:22,870
"I can't with this house. It's too scary."

805
00:29:25,350 --> 00:29:25,870
You know?!

806
00:29:26,010 --> 00:29:26,750
Huh?

807
00:29:27,340 --> 00:29:28,370
Oh, I mean,

808
00:29:28,390 --> 00:29:30,190
your acting was so good.

809
00:29:30,520 --> 00:29:32,330
You frustrated me so much that

810
00:29:32,350 --> 00:29:34,770
I really felt like killing you, Mr. Dax.

811
00:29:34,790 --> 00:29:35,510
Wow.

812
00:29:38,270 --> 00:29:39,140
What's the matter?

813
00:29:39,640 --> 00:29:40,390
I'm flattered.

814
00:29:40,510 --> 00:29:43,350
Getting a compliment from
my beloved superstar

815
00:29:43,440 --> 00:29:44,630
really made my day.

816
00:29:45,240 --> 00:29:46,990
By the way,
which scene should we do next?

817
00:29:47,400 --> 00:29:48,430
Let's go with...

818
00:29:48,560 --> 00:29:49,510
the dismemberment part.

819
00:29:49,920 --> 00:29:52,150
I want to practice the movements.

820
00:29:52,170 --> 00:29:52,870
Alright.

821
00:29:52,970 --> 00:29:54,470
What kind of corpse would you like?

822
00:29:55,070 --> 00:29:57,500
A fresh, still-twitching corpse?

823
00:30:02,490 --> 00:30:03,110
Or...

824
00:30:03,310 --> 00:30:05,180
a long-dead, bloated corpse?

825
00:30:08,200 --> 00:30:09,180
Which do you prefer?

826
00:30:11,680 --> 00:30:13,310
Stay still like a corpse would.

827
00:30:14,040 --> 00:30:15,060
Leave that to me.

828
00:30:17,360 --> 00:30:20,140
Why do I have to go in there?

829
00:30:20,160 --> 00:30:20,930
I do not want to go inside.

830
00:30:20,950 --> 00:30:22,430
I am scared of ghosts.

831
00:30:22,590 --> 00:30:24,930
Grandpa, you're a ghost. Why are you
even scared of ghosts?

832
00:30:24,950 --> 00:30:27,690
Ghosts can be scared of ghosts, too.

833
00:30:28,300 --> 00:30:30,340
I do not want to see anything gory.

834
00:30:30,360 --> 00:30:31,750
Grandpa...

835
00:30:36,230 --> 00:30:37,640
You are worried about your friend, right?

836
00:30:37,660 --> 00:30:38,490
Yes!

837
00:30:39,220 --> 00:30:39,690
Fine.

838
00:30:40,000 --> 00:30:40,890
I will go in there.

839
00:30:41,350 --> 00:30:42,660
Let me close my eyes first.

840
00:30:52,230 --> 00:30:53,310
What are you doing to Dax?

841
00:30:58,320 --> 00:30:59,160
Is that blood...?

842
00:31:07,710 --> 00:31:08,640
I cannot take it anymore.

843
00:31:20,440 --> 00:31:21,070
Wow.

844
00:31:21,400 --> 00:31:22,310
How was it?

845
00:31:22,960 --> 00:31:24,230
Is it as realistic as you wanted it to be?

846
00:31:24,870 --> 00:31:26,940
Using sauce as blood

847
00:31:26,960 --> 00:31:28,690
really helps build the emotion, huh?

848
00:31:28,710 --> 00:31:30,270
Now I understand...

849
00:31:30,290 --> 00:31:32,950
the thrill psycho killers feel
when dismembering a body.

850
00:31:33,000 --> 00:31:35,870
I told you
I'm a professional supporting actor.

851
00:31:35,890 --> 00:31:38,270
I have a bunch of other tricks
to share with you.

852
00:31:39,160 --> 00:31:40,140
Please share them.

853
00:31:40,520 --> 00:31:43,140
You really helped me out today.

854
00:31:44,080 --> 00:31:45,960
Oh, I've got a concert coming up.

855
00:31:46,080 --> 00:31:49,310
I'll save a seat just for you, then.

856
00:31:49,740 --> 00:31:50,220
Yes!

857
00:31:50,240 --> 00:31:51,870
Oh, thank you so much.

858
00:31:52,320 --> 00:31:54,030
I have to practice my dance moves now.

859
00:31:54,320 --> 00:31:55,350
Thank you.

860
00:31:56,000 --> 00:31:56,940
I'll go clean up first.

861
00:32:22,440 --> 00:32:23,590
This tastes good.

862
00:32:24,510 --> 00:32:27,430
He really is a psycho killer.

863
00:32:31,110 --> 00:32:31,830
Ugh.

864
00:32:32,340 --> 00:32:34,080
Where did Dax go?

865
00:32:37,390 --> 00:32:38,830
Do not tell me...

866
00:32:38,990 --> 00:32:40,140
That suitc...

867
00:32:40,890 --> 00:32:44,030
I cannot stay here any longer!

868
00:32:52,310 --> 00:32:53,510
- So?
- Dobby!

869
00:32:53,890 --> 00:32:54,680
Dax...

870
00:32:54,930 --> 00:32:56,510
Dax is dead!

871
00:32:57,320 --> 00:32:59,960
He was chopped up into bite-sized pieces

872
00:32:59,990 --> 00:33:01,510
and shoved into a suitcase!

873
00:33:02,310 --> 00:33:04,150
Dax is dead!

874
00:33:04,260 --> 00:33:06,090
- Dax is dead, Grandpa?
- Yeah.

875
00:33:06,150 --> 00:33:07,860
Mr. Dobby... Mr. Dobby!

876
00:33:08,030 --> 00:33:08,940
Mr. Dobby!

877
00:33:09,130 --> 00:33:11,130
Mr. Dobby. Mr. Dobby.

878
00:33:11,490 --> 00:33:12,300
Mr. Dobby.

879
00:33:14,870 --> 00:33:16,010
What's wrong, Mr. Dobby?

880
00:33:18,210 --> 00:33:19,580
I talked to Dollar.

881
00:33:19,900 --> 00:33:21,900
He said that the police are on their way.

882
00:33:22,240 --> 00:33:23,250
He told us to hang on a second.

883
00:33:23,270 --> 00:33:24,550
- Hang on?
- Yes.

884
00:33:24,990 --> 00:33:25,790
I still have to?

885
00:33:26,640 --> 00:33:27,630
I'm not gonna wait anymore!

886
00:33:27,650 --> 00:33:28,850
Whoa!

887
00:33:30,800 --> 00:33:31,430
What?

888
00:33:31,990 --> 00:33:33,010
Who are you?

889
00:33:33,030 --> 00:33:33,990
Why did you come in here?

890
00:33:37,250 --> 00:33:38,910
Shut up, you murderer!

891
00:33:38,950 --> 00:33:39,870
What murderer...?

892
00:33:40,590 --> 00:33:41,520
Mr. Dobby, be careful!

893
00:33:42,450 --> 00:33:43,030
Don't move...

894
00:33:45,390 --> 00:33:46,030
Dobby.

895
00:33:46,070 --> 00:33:47,270
Dax...

896
00:33:47,900 --> 00:33:49,350
is in that suitcase.

897
00:33:50,590 --> 00:33:51,850
Why did you kill my friend?

898
00:33:51,870 --> 00:33:55,750
♫I love you so, so much♫

899
00:33:55,880 --> 00:33:57,380
I didn't kill...

900
00:33:57,400 --> 00:33:58,910
You're still lying, huh?!

901
00:33:59,350 --> 00:34:01,830
You killed him and
shoved him into that suitcase, didn't you?!

902
00:34:01,850 --> 00:34:02,490
There!

903
00:34:02,510 --> 00:34:09,030
♫Cutie pie, I only think of you♫

904
00:34:09,080 --> 00:34:10,260
Ow...

905
00:34:12,260 --> 00:34:13,250
Are you gonna grab the knife?!

906
00:34:14,120 --> 00:34:15,230
You are, aren't you?

907
00:34:15,260 --> 00:34:16,790
Not dead...

908
00:34:16,850 --> 00:34:17,790
Fine, then...

909
00:34:17,830 --> 00:34:19,070
die!

910
00:34:19,100 --> 00:34:21,570
♫I want to tell you, I want to embrace you♫

911
00:34:21,590 --> 00:34:23,750
♫You cutie pie♫

912
00:34:23,880 --> 00:34:24,870
How does that feel?!

913
00:34:26,590 --> 00:34:27,449
Dax...

914
00:34:27,469 --> 00:34:28,389
Dax...

915
00:34:28,699 --> 00:34:29,739
Dax...

916
00:34:30,320 --> 00:34:32,739
How am I gonna tell your parents about this?

917
00:34:33,280 --> 00:34:34,630
Dax, I'm sorry...

918
00:34:35,000 --> 00:34:39,150
♫I love you the way you are, my cutie pie♫

919
00:34:39,650 --> 00:34:41,480
My supporting actor.

920
00:34:41,500 --> 00:34:42,550
Dax!

921
00:34:43,820 --> 00:34:44,940
Dax.

922
00:34:46,040 --> 00:34:46,909
Dax...

923
00:34:48,280 --> 00:34:49,540
Dax...

924
00:34:49,760 --> 00:34:50,630
Why are you calling my name?

925
00:34:55,679 --> 00:34:56,449
Huh?

926
00:34:57,650 --> 00:34:58,550
He is still alive?

927
00:34:58,850 --> 00:34:59,470
Dax?

928
00:34:59,490 --> 00:35:00,470
You're still alive?

929
00:35:00,790 --> 00:35:01,670
What are you saying?

930
00:35:05,280 --> 00:35:06,150
Mr. Disney?!

931
00:35:06,840 --> 00:35:07,580
- Huh?
- Huh?

932
00:35:07,600 --> 00:35:08,710
- Disney?!
- Mr. Disney?

933
00:35:08,750 --> 00:35:09,630
Disney who?

934
00:35:09,650 --> 00:35:10,910
Disney, you know?

935
00:35:18,890 --> 00:35:19,630
He's...

936
00:35:19,660 --> 00:35:23,350
Mr. Disney, the five-time winner of
the People's Choice Award!

937
00:35:25,510 --> 00:35:27,110
I punched him five times...

938
00:35:27,830 --> 00:35:28,720
Hey, Mr. Disney...

939
00:35:28,740 --> 00:35:29,910
Mr. Disney...

940
00:35:30,830 --> 00:35:34,630
The beloved superstar sure took a beating.

941
00:35:38,820 --> 00:35:39,910
When will you eat?

942
00:35:40,650 --> 00:35:41,790
Your eyes are better now, aren't they?

943
00:35:43,460 --> 00:35:43,960
Just.

944
00:35:43,990 --> 00:35:44,570
Give.

945
00:35:44,600 --> 00:35:45,190
Up.

946
00:35:45,400 --> 00:35:48,320
If you're gonna cough like that,
you might as well just go tell him.

947
00:35:48,800 --> 00:35:49,760
If I eat it,

948
00:35:50,060 --> 00:35:51,940
can you promise you'll stay with me?

949
00:35:53,580 --> 00:35:54,800
You'll hold my hand

950
00:35:55,420 --> 00:35:56,860
wherever I want to go.

951
00:35:56,880 --> 00:35:57,650
Alright.

952
00:35:58,340 --> 00:35:59,680
I promise.

953
00:35:59,940 --> 00:36:00,710
Now eat!

954
00:36:09,350 --> 00:36:10,010
- Whoa!
- What?!

955
00:36:10,030 --> 00:36:10,890
- Whoa!
- Hey!

956
00:36:10,910 --> 00:36:12,350
Why did you eat it? Spit it out!

957
00:36:12,370 --> 00:36:13,110
You're gonna die!

958
00:36:14,100 --> 00:36:14,760
Spit it out!

959
00:36:15,380 --> 00:36:16,020
Spit it out!

960
00:36:16,850 --> 00:36:17,690
Not gonna spit it out, huh?

961
00:36:17,710 --> 00:36:18,790
Take this!

962
00:36:31,390 --> 00:36:32,270
Po,

963
00:36:32,560 --> 00:36:33,740
you traitor.

964
00:36:33,920 --> 00:36:35,590
You know full well I'm scared of ghosts.

965
00:36:35,610 --> 00:36:38,240
How dare you help him

966
00:36:38,450 --> 00:36:39,910
trick me into being his caretaker?

967
00:36:40,140 --> 00:36:40,950
Well...

968
00:36:41,160 --> 00:36:42,910
I already agreed to help him,

969
00:36:43,000 --> 00:36:44,910
so I have to keep my promise.

970
00:36:45,280 --> 00:36:47,990
Aren't you glad?
Your little brother keeps his word.

971
00:36:49,620 --> 00:36:51,110
Didn't you say you'd get 2,000?

972
00:36:52,140 --> 00:36:53,230
- Shut it.
- Oh.

973
00:36:54,620 --> 00:36:56,910
I did as you asked. I ate it.

974
00:36:57,030 --> 00:36:58,850
Now you have to keep your promise.

975
00:36:59,440 --> 00:37:01,150
You still have the nerve to ask me that?

976
00:37:01,380 --> 00:37:02,550
Seriously,

977
00:37:02,860 --> 00:37:03,990
what the hell is wrong with you?

978
00:37:04,400 --> 00:37:06,110
You're so obsessed with seeing ghosts.

979
00:37:07,250 --> 00:37:07,940
Or...

980
00:37:08,410 --> 00:37:10,480
you can't trick others
by being a phony fortune teller anymore,

981
00:37:10,740 --> 00:37:12,510
so you've decided to be a shaman instead?

982
00:37:17,030 --> 00:37:18,070
I have my reasons.

983
00:37:18,180 --> 00:37:20,140
It doesn't matter why you did this.

984
00:37:20,450 --> 00:37:22,470
You can't go around
harassing people like this.

985
00:37:23,710 --> 00:37:25,620
If you keep this up,

986
00:37:26,150 --> 00:37:28,590
I don't think we can share a dorm anymore.

987
00:37:44,660 --> 00:37:45,550
I want to see my mom!

988
00:37:50,310 --> 00:37:51,900
I want to see ghosts...

989
00:37:53,500 --> 00:37:54,830
because I want to see my mom.

990
00:37:57,940 --> 00:37:59,870
My mom passed away on the day I was born.

991
00:38:04,470 --> 00:38:07,020
Dad blamed me for her death,
saying I was a jinx.

992
00:38:08,740 --> 00:38:10,580
My relatives also think I'm a jinx.

993
00:38:15,650 --> 00:38:17,310
Life has been pretty harsh on you,

994
00:38:18,560 --> 00:38:20,070
but I think they're right.

995
00:38:20,880 --> 00:38:22,450
See? Even when you're alone,

996
00:38:22,480 --> 00:38:24,050
you still manage to get into trouble.

997
00:38:24,680 --> 00:38:26,190
Stop talking.

998
00:38:26,440 --> 00:38:27,190
Give me your hand.

999
00:38:27,210 --> 00:38:27,990
I don't want it.

1000
00:38:29,820 --> 00:38:31,270
I want to see her

1001
00:38:33,950 --> 00:38:35,580
and ask her...

1002
00:38:37,250 --> 00:38:39,350
if I was the one who killed her.

1003
00:38:43,270 --> 00:38:44,390
Are you done?

1004
00:38:45,650 --> 00:38:46,710
If you're done, leave.

1005
00:38:47,910 --> 00:38:48,750
Oh, wow...

1006
00:38:49,360 --> 00:38:50,120
Dang it, Daeng.

1007
00:38:50,340 --> 00:38:53,040
I never knew you could be so heartless.

1008
00:38:53,060 --> 00:38:54,910
His life is already hard enough.
Why push him away?

1009
00:38:55,220 --> 00:38:56,070
You meanie!

1010
00:38:56,240 --> 00:38:56,790
Cruel!

1011
00:38:57,110 --> 00:38:57,630
Heartless!

1012
00:38:57,650 --> 00:38:58,510
Toxic!

1013
00:38:59,070 --> 00:39:01,250
♫You're toxic, I'm slippin'...♫

1014
00:39:01,620 --> 00:39:02,240
What's this?

1015
00:39:02,260 --> 00:39:03,000
The steamed bun from earlier.

1016
00:39:05,060 --> 00:39:06,580
If you don't want to help,

1017
00:39:07,830 --> 00:39:09,650
I won't bother you anymore.

1018
00:39:11,030 --> 00:39:11,590
Hey,

1019
00:39:12,680 --> 00:39:14,070
when did I say I wouldn't help?

1020
00:39:15,070 --> 00:39:16,390
Well, you told me to leave.

1021
00:39:20,700 --> 00:39:21,790
I meant, "Let's go,

1022
00:39:25,190 --> 00:39:26,550
let's look for your mother."

1023
00:39:27,800 --> 00:39:28,280
Hey...

1024
00:39:39,300 --> 00:39:40,850
But if we find your mom,

1025
00:39:41,520 --> 00:39:42,870
you'll have to talk to her yourself.

1026
00:39:43,790 --> 00:39:44,800
I'm scared of ghosts.

1027
00:39:46,600 --> 00:39:47,990
If you're scared of ghosts,

1028
00:39:48,860 --> 00:39:50,150
I'll cover your eyes.

1029
00:39:56,910 --> 00:39:57,650
Is this better?

1030
00:39:58,110 --> 00:39:58,960
Hey!

1031
00:39:58,980 --> 00:40:00,110
What are you doing?

1032
00:40:00,950 --> 00:40:02,110
Are you trying to blind me or something?

1033
00:40:03,040 --> 00:40:03,990
But you're scared of ghosts?

1034
00:40:04,740 --> 00:40:06,500
I can take care of myself.

1035
00:40:07,120 --> 00:40:08,510
If you want to see them, go ahead.

1036
00:40:16,990 --> 00:40:17,510
I'll give it my all.

1037
00:40:17,680 --> 00:40:19,590
Thank you for encouraging me.

1038
00:40:21,800 --> 00:40:22,590
I'm gonna cut your fingers off.

1039
00:40:22,660 --> 00:40:23,910
What encouragement? Give me 2,000.

1040
00:40:24,050 --> 00:40:25,120
Mm, that's right.

1041
00:40:25,890 --> 00:40:26,550
See?

1042
00:40:26,590 --> 00:40:27,410
Give him 500, too.

1043
00:40:27,430 --> 00:40:29,060
No, you still owe me 500.

1044
00:40:29,310 --> 00:40:30,630
- We're gonna share it.
- Oh...

1045
00:40:35,640 --> 00:40:37,710
I'm so sorry, Mr. Disney.

1046
00:40:37,830 --> 00:40:40,910
I thought you were
the dismemberment killer from the news.

1047
00:40:41,480 --> 00:40:42,470
It's alright.

1048
00:40:43,430 --> 00:40:45,390
It's partly my fault, too.

1049
00:40:45,650 --> 00:40:48,800
I was acting suspicious,
and that made things worse.

1050
00:40:55,060 --> 00:40:55,710
Oh.

1051
00:40:56,590 --> 00:40:57,310
Whoa.

1052
00:40:57,650 --> 00:40:59,310
I'm really sorry, Mr. Disney.

1053
00:40:59,480 --> 00:41:00,550
Ugh...

1054
00:41:00,860 --> 00:41:01,840
I'm sorry.

1055
00:41:03,980 --> 00:41:04,850
By the way...

1056
00:41:05,180 --> 00:41:07,950
did you need something
from the room owner?

1057
00:41:08,180 --> 00:41:08,790
Oh...

1058
00:41:09,500 --> 00:41:11,150
Can you take a look...

1059
00:41:11,560 --> 00:41:12,630
at this video?

1060
00:41:18,590 --> 00:41:20,270
Is this your manager?

1061
00:41:20,930 --> 00:41:22,270
No, this isn't my manager.

1062
00:41:22,440 --> 00:41:23,190
- Huh?
- What?

1063
00:41:24,600 --> 00:41:25,510
That's me.

1064
00:41:25,540 --> 00:41:26,280
- Huh?
- Huh?

1065
00:41:27,120 --> 00:41:28,590
I remember this box.

1066
00:41:28,980 --> 00:41:31,550
On that day, I came to put my things away.

1067
00:41:34,550 --> 00:41:35,470
We found him!

1068
00:41:35,510 --> 00:41:36,730
Finally...

1069
00:41:36,750 --> 00:41:39,750
I've found your relative, Gaysorn!

1070
00:41:43,140 --> 00:41:43,990
Mr. Disney,

1071
00:41:45,300 --> 00:41:46,890
do you have a relative...

1072
00:41:46,910 --> 00:41:47,910
named Gaysorn?

1073
00:41:49,740 --> 00:41:50,830
Gaysorn...

1074
00:41:59,470 --> 00:42:00,910
- No.
- Oh.

1075
00:42:01,070 --> 00:42:01,950
No, huh...

1076
00:42:02,270 --> 00:42:04,230
Mr. Dax already asked me about this once.

1077
00:42:04,350 --> 00:42:06,710
I called my manager to ask them about this.

1078
00:42:07,480 --> 00:42:09,430
Oh, but they said...

1079
00:42:09,920 --> 00:42:10,550
Yeah?

1080
00:42:11,060 --> 00:42:11,710
What did they say?

1081
00:42:11,880 --> 00:42:13,870
They don't have any relatives
named Gaysorn either.

1082
00:42:14,390 --> 00:42:15,790
- Why did he say "but," then?
- Right?

1083
00:42:17,070 --> 00:42:17,740
Oh!

1084
00:42:18,360 --> 00:42:19,350
Mr. Disney,

1085
00:42:19,430 --> 00:42:20,650
the thing is...

1086
00:42:20,670 --> 00:42:23,310
the video was recorded on the day
my grandpa passed away.

1087
00:42:23,600 --> 00:42:27,310
In the footage,
you were walking up the stairs

1088
00:42:27,430 --> 00:42:29,350
when you dropped Grandma Gaysorn's photo.

1089
00:42:29,670 --> 00:42:31,030
Are you sure you're not her relative?

1090
00:42:31,140 --> 00:42:32,590
That photo isn't mine, though.

1091
00:42:32,820 --> 00:42:33,590
- What?
- Huh?

1092
00:42:34,850 --> 00:42:36,830
It came falling down from upstairs.

1093
00:42:37,030 --> 00:42:38,150
Where did it come from, then?

1094
00:42:39,870 --> 00:42:40,670
Wait, wait, wait.

1095
00:42:42,050 --> 00:42:44,910
I think I know who dropped that photo.

1096
00:42:45,280 --> 00:42:46,990
On that day,
I went up to the fourth floor

1097
00:42:47,140 --> 00:42:48,870
and saw a woman...

1098
00:42:48,950 --> 00:42:50,880
carrying a whole bunch of things.

1099
00:42:51,300 --> 00:42:53,230
I think she was the one who dropped the photo.

1100
00:42:55,060 --> 00:42:56,150
There's a female ghost in our dorm, too?

1101
00:42:56,300 --> 00:42:57,040
Hm?

1102
00:42:58,000 --> 00:42:59,000
I think she's human.

1103
00:42:59,030 --> 00:43:00,310
Just Grandpa's ghost is enough.

1104
00:43:02,600 --> 00:43:03,550
A woman...

1105
00:43:04,720 --> 00:43:05,460
Who?

1106
00:43:05,480 --> 00:43:07,600
I think she's the manager of this dorm.

1107
00:43:07,830 --> 00:43:08,950
Her name is Danis.

1108
00:43:09,190 --> 00:43:09,910
- Huh?!
- Huh?!

1109
00:43:11,270 --> 00:43:12,270
Danis?

1110
00:43:12,820 --> 00:43:14,790
How could it be her?

1111
00:43:26,410 --> 00:43:28,920
Why is this ice cream seller
dressed like that?

1112
00:43:29,120 --> 00:43:31,000
It is like he is from the Joseon era.

1113
00:43:36,300 --> 00:43:37,300
Delta,

1114
00:43:37,720 --> 00:43:38,560
do you remember me?

1115
00:43:38,580 --> 00:43:39,720
Dolly Darling?

1116
00:43:39,740 --> 00:43:40,720
Delta Oppa?

1117
00:43:40,740 --> 00:43:42,240
Hey, I thought you had forgotten about me.

1118
00:43:42,260 --> 00:43:43,680
They call each other by their nicknames.

1119
00:43:43,920 --> 00:43:45,050
Are they really just friends?

1120
00:43:47,760 --> 00:43:48,880
When you talked to Danis,

1121
00:43:48,900 --> 00:43:50,640
she said that the box she was carrying

1122
00:43:50,660 --> 00:43:51,920
belonged to the director of the orphanage.

1123
00:43:52,080 --> 00:43:53,200
Where?

1124
00:43:53,220 --> 00:43:54,400
Where is Grandma Gaysorn's photo?

1125
00:43:55,240 --> 00:43:57,520
Is this the photo?
I can't even see her face.

1126
00:43:57,580 --> 00:43:58,980
You should call the director

1127
00:43:59,000 --> 00:44:00,960
and ask her if this photo is hers.

1128
00:44:00,980 --> 00:44:02,560
It's probably too late to call her now.

1129
00:44:02,580 --> 00:44:03,240
- Huh?
- Huh?

1130
00:44:05,120 --> 00:44:05,800
Don't tell me...

1131
00:44:08,640 --> 00:44:12,120
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

1132
00:44:12,200 --> 00:44:15,880
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

1133
00:44:18,440 --> 00:44:23,920
♫Every step we take has a meaning♫

1134
00:44:25,670 --> 00:44:30,560
♫No path is ever meaningless♫

1135
00:44:32,800 --> 00:44:38,940
♫As long as our hearts keep searching♫

1136
00:44:39,880 --> 00:44:44,440
♫One day, we'll find
what we're yearning for♫

1137
00:44:44,460 --> 00:44:48,000
♫Walking alone is fine,
but it's better when you're by my side♫

1138
00:44:48,020 --> 00:44:51,620
♫It won't be lonely
when you're here to walk beside♫

1139
00:44:51,640 --> 00:44:55,160
♫Like a love that waits, waits at the D Dorm♫

1140
00:44:55,180 --> 00:44:57,460
♫Like a love that remains,
remains at the dorm♫

1141
00:44:57,480 --> 00:45:04,360
♫Meaningful love and good things
await on every path♫

1142
00:45:04,540 --> 00:45:11,280
♫It might not be a coincidence
that we get to meet♫

1143
00:45:11,750 --> 00:45:18,900
♫There might be hidden meanings
on the path beneath our feet♫

1144
00:45:18,920 --> 00:45:25,970
♫Perhaps the D Dorm
is what led me to meet you♫

1145
00:45:25,990 --> 00:45:29,590
[The D Dorm]
